  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The corrected baseline’s objective and effective endpoint weight are unknown. Calling 0.75 an increase is premature: it could increase, decrease or reproduce the baseline weighting. Establish the exact reduction and realized group counts from the supplied baseline; published implementations cannot resolve this local fact.",
    "The experiment is not fully reproducible. Specify endpoint-prefix sampling, group sizes, reconstruction eligibility, mask-count and empty-mask policies, truncation, and treatment of terminal positions within ordinary reconstruction. The pseudocode also omits the baseline/control arms, checkpoint selection rule and concrete compute allocations.",
    "The report preserves within-group reductions but does not establish whether the baseline loss decomposes into independent group losses. Batch-coupled losses or regularizers require explicit treatment; summing two separately computed group losses could change more than weighting.",
    "Electronics’ single-negative training margins do not establish a right-context problem. A small fixed matched-target context probe could support this hypothesis, but its cost must be budgeted. Endpoint weighting remains a reasonable first experiment without claiming that it addresses compatibility or immediate usefulness.",
    "Originality 3/10 is reasonable. Potential 6/10 is provisional, and difficulty 3/10 assumes the baseline already exposes compatible groups. Require paired validation comparisons when available, disclose validation queries, and freeze checkpoint/configuration selection before held-out evaluation. User bootstrap intervals cannot measure seed variability or adaptive search bias.",
    "The related-work descriptions lack precise bibliographic details and verified implementation evidence. Excluding DualRec is a conservative design choice; multiple jointly trained internal branches are not automatically independent-model ensembles under the stated constraint."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Verify established endpoint supervision and its implementation before attributing novelty to the proposed weighting. This informs the literature comparison; the host baseline still requires separate documentation.",
      "query": "In BERT4Rec: Sequential Recommendation with Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformer (2019), how do the paper and authors' released implementation construct last-item-only training examples versus ordinary masked reconstruction? Identify their sampling proportions, masked-target loss reduction, truncation and appended-mask inference, distinguishing paper statements from implementation behavior."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether the proposed coefficient has relevant precedent and whether the context-mismatch explanation has controlled empirical support. This may strengthen the rationale or identify a cheaper diagnostic before training.",
      "query": "Which sequential recommendation studies explicitly compare terminal-mask or prefix-only supervision with interior bidirectional masked-item reconstruction in one jointly trained BERT4Rec-style model? Look for fixed weighted-loss ablations, controls for masking frequency and loss normalization, and evidence linking right-context dependence to next-item ranking. Include the 2022 Disentangling Past-Future Modeling in Sequential Recommendation via Dual Networks paper and distinguish its diagnosis from its architecture."
    }
  ]
}
